*Diagram to be drawn by the candidate.* A model drawing contains, all labelled:

- a **stand** with a **clamp** holding a **burette vertically**; the burette contains the dilute HCl and has a tap (stop-cock) at the bottom;
- under the burette tip, a **conical flask** containing $25\ \text{cm}^3$ of $0.25\ \text{M}$ NaOH (measured with the pipette) and 3 drops of **phenolphthalein**;
- a white tile (or white paper) under the flask so that the colour change is easy to see;
- the acid is run into the flask while the flask is swirled.
